Description: real-time interface traffic of network devices over SNMP
 Anemobit reads interface counters from a device over SNMP and shows the
 download and upload rates with gauges and a five-minute chart, in the
 system tray (with the rate in the top bar on Ubuntu) and in a main window.
 .
 It works with devices that provide the standard IF-MIB with 64-bit
 interface counters over SNMPv2c or SNMPv3 (authentication: MD5, SHA1,
 SHA224, SHA256, SHA384, SHA512; privacy: DES, AES-128). Passwords are kept
 in the Secret Service keyring.
